{"name":"Snow Globe","hex":"#f4f2e9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snow globe","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A decorative object or toy containing a model of a landscape, fluid and suspended white flakes that emulate snowfall when shaken."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snow_globe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snowglobe (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Snowglobe is a 2007 television film directed by Ron Lagomarsino and starring Christina Milian, Josh Cooke and Matt Keeslar. The film was produced by ABC Family and first aired on December 15, 2007, in their 25 Days of Christmas programming block."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/Snowglobe_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowglobe_(film)"},{"title":"Snowglobe (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Snowglobe is an American musical group based in the southern United States. While their music covers a range of styles and genres, they are generally referred to as an indie rock group. The band has had a rotating cast over the years, but the primary members are currently Brad Postlethwaite, Nahshon Benford, Jeff Hulett (drums), Tim Regan, Brandon Robertson (bass), and Luke White."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ad/Snowglobe-icon.jpg/330px-Snowglobe-icon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowglobe_(band)"},{"title":"Snow globe","blocks":[{"text":"A snow globe is a transparent sphere or spheroid, traditionally made of glass, enclosing a miniaturized scene of some sort, often together with a model of a town, neighborhood, landscape or figure. The sphere also encloses the water in the globe; the water serves as the medium through which the \"snow\" falls. To activate the snow, the globe is shaken to churn up the white particles. The globe is then placed back in its position and the flakes fall down slowly through the water. Snow globes sometimes have a built-in music box that plays a song. Some snow globes have a design around the outer base for decoration. Snow globes are often used as a collectible item."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Santa_snow_globe.jpg/330px-Santa_snow_globe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow_globe"},{"title":"Snow","blocks":[{"text":"Snow is a form of solid atmospheric precipitation consisting of individual ice crystals that grow while suspended in the air—usually within clouds—and then fall, accumulating on the ground, where they undergo further changes. It consists of frozen crystalline water throughout its life cycle, starting when, under suitable conditions, the ice crystals form in the atmosphere, increase to millimeter size, precipitate and accumulate on surfaces, then metamorphose in place, and ultimately melt, slide, or sublimate away."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg/330px-CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Australian_Souvenir_Snow_Globes.jpg/500px-Australian_Souvenir_Snow_Globes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Australian_Souvenir_Snow_Globes.jpg/1280px-Australian_Souvenir_Snow_Globes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Australian_Souvenir_Snow_Globes.jpg/500px-Australian_Souvenir_Snow_Globes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Plastic Australian souvenir snow globes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAustralian_Souvenir_Snow_Globes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Snow_Globe_girl_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Snow_Globe_girl_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3e/Snow_Globe_girl_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Snow_Globe_girl_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Snow_Globe_girl_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A girl holding a snow globe","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASnow_Globe_girl_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/500px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/1280px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/500px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Extratropical cyclonic snowstorm, February 24, 2007—(Click for animation.)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFeb242007_blizzard.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Snowsquall_line-Bourrasque_neige_frontal_NOAA.png/500px-Snowsquall_line-Bourrasque_neige_frontal_NOAA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Snowsquall_line-Bourrasque_neige_frontal_NOAA.png/500px-Snowsquall_line-Bourrasque_neige_frontal_NOAA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u